I think part of the problem is in the fact that the game allows you to
become a walking tank. Or, to put it in a different and a more exact way,
I think some of the monsters are not dangerous enough at all. I think
the biggest let-downs are the barrow-wights and the nazguls. These are
both from Tolkien and neither of them have any of the special abilities
that Tolkien used. Mostly, the fear effect is lacking. I believe this
should be easy to implement. It would resemble a stun, with two additional
effects: 1) on any turn that you're terribly afraid, you're likely to
be rendered immobile for a number of turns. 2) You move as if you're
stunned, but if the move you take would make you attack the nazgul or
barrow wight, you would be immobile and get a message along the lines of
"The frightul presence of the <monster> overwhelms you!".

At the moment, neither of these monsters poses any danger. There are many
other monsters that are just way too easy to kill. I would like, for example,
a certain number of demons (3?) to be able to intentionally summon help if
they realise that their attacks or special attacks aren't getting through.
Also, some of the demons are supposed to be very, very big, and it would
be great if they could stun you and so on.

Also, I don't think a silver dragon scale mail should reflect anything
if you're wearing a cloak on top of it.

